      "writtenOn": "2024-04-23T23:22:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the key thing is there, by handling IDLE state here, you don\u0027t have to use the state machine any more\n\nonly risk I see is when `bta_dm_sdp_callback` runs on different thread, then you have to schedule the state check and `bta_dm_free_sdp_db` after do_in_main_thread\n\nHence, would we have `bta_dm_sdp_callback` be like:\n\n```\nstatic void bta_dm_sdp_callback(const RawAddress\u0026 /* bd_addr */,\n                                tSDP_STATUS sdp_status) {\n  do_in_main_thread(FROM_HERE, [sdp_status] {\n    log::info(\"{}\", bta_dm_state_text(bta_dm_discovery_get_state()));\n    if (bta_dm_discovery_get_state() \u003d\u003d BTA_DM_DISCOVER_IDLE) {\n      bta_dm_free_sdp_db();\n      return;\n    }\n    bta_dm_sdp_result(sdp_status);\n  }                           \n}\n```\n\nThis more accurately reflect what the previous version of code was doing",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 382,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 385,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "783de1dc73f34216238d11f821aa2a6b22b56121",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ea43a81_8dccc6d7",
        "filename": "system/bta/dm/bta_dm_disc.cc",
